# The production host's front door (D346). Caddy gets and renews the https
# certificate for APP_DOMAIN by itself, redirects http to https, and forwards
# every request to nginx (the `web` container), which serves the page and
# forwards /api/* to the orchestrator.
#
# The client's address: Caddy writes X-Forwarded-For itself and drops one the
# client sent (no `trusted_proxies` here), nginx appends Caddy's address, and
# the orchestrator reads past exactly these two hops (TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=2,
# scripts/prod-env.sh). One proxy more or less here means changing that number.
#
# Security headers are nginx's (infra/docker/security-headers.conf), the same
# file CI checks on every PR - not repeated here, so there is one place to change.

# No admin API: by default Caddy listens on localhost:2019 inside its container
# for configuration changes. Nothing here uses it - the file is the whole
# configuration, and a restart reloads it - so it is off rather than trusted
# to stay unreachable.
{
	admin off
}

{$APP_DOMAIN} {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy web:80
}
